paragraph start
name: paragraph-tp-marks-kinds
A mark says: this block matters for a purpose. Kinds: rule, step,
fact, check and card. A rule goes to the rule list. A check is a
yes or no item for a checklist. A step goes into a track. A fact
and a card feed a fact sheet and a card deck. A kind is a
.blocktype file, so a new kind needs no code.
contract start
id: q1deb06
question: Is this one idea a reader could restate?
contract end
answer start
for: q1deb06
asked: Is this one idea a reader could restate?

answer end
paragraph end

paragraph start
name: paragraph-tp-marks-where
Where: a whole file, a chapter or one block. Marking a chapter
marks everything inside it, in order. Marking a file marks the
file as one item.
contract start
id: q1deb06
question: Is this one idea a reader could restate?
contract end
answer start
for: q1deb06
asked: Is this one idea a reader could restate?

answer end
